# Frontend conventions

Apply on any work in `frontend/` (and on new code in this repo when the context is UI).

**Questions vs tasks:** `.cursor/rules/ask-dont-implement.mdc` — opinion / “how should we…” → answer only; implement when the user asks to change code.

## Functions and components

- **Always arrow functions** for components, hooks, and utilities in `frontend/src`.
- Export as: `export const Component = () => …`, `export const useFoo = () => …`, `export const helper = () => …`.
- Do not use `export function Name() { … }` unless unavoidable (e.g. type overloads — rare).

```tsx
// ✅
export const EntryPage = () => <div />;
export const usePwaInstall = () => { /* hooks */ };

// ❌
export function EntryPage() { return <div />; }
```

Keep types as `type` / `interface` — not arrow-style.

## Exports

- **Export only what other files import** — functions, components, hooks, types, constants.
- **File-local** — no `export` if used only inside the same file (`type AuthSession`, helper parsers, private constants).
- **Before adding `export`** — check call sites (`Grep`); don't export "for later" or mirror every internal type in the public API.
- **`export type`** — only when another file imports that type; otherwise plain `type`.

```ts
// ✅ authApi.ts — types stay local; only callers are exported
type AuthSession = { token: string };
export const loginUser = (): Promise<AuthSession> => …;

// ✅ authTypes.ts — form types imported by hook + validator
export type LoginFormValues = { email: string; password: string };

// ✅ authScreen.ts — screen ids in types/, not config/
export const AUTH_SCREEN = { LOGIN: "login", REGISTER: "register" } as const;
export type AuthScreen = (typeof AUTH_SCREEN)[keyof typeof AUTH_SCREEN];

// ❌ export type AuthSession when nothing outside authApi.ts imports it
export type AuthSession = { … };
```

## Comments

- In **`.ts` / `.tsx`** — line comments `//` only, not `/** … */` / `/* … */`.
- Single line: `// explanation`
- Multiple lines — each with `//`, not a block JSDoc.
- In **`.css`** keep `/* … */` (different syntax).

```ts
// ✅
// Phone or tablet — not desktop.
export const isMobileBrowser = (): boolean => { … };

// ❌
/** Phone or tablet */
export const isMobileBrowser = (): boolean => { … };
```

Comments are for non-obvious logic only; do not repeat what the code already shows.

## Language

- **English only** for all user-facing copy in `frontend/`: UI labels, headings, placeholders, buttons, validation/error messages, `aria-label` / `title`, empty states, and `index.html` `lang`.
- Code identifiers, comments, and commit messages stay in English too.
- No Ukrainian (or other locale strings) in source until i18n is explicitly added.

```tsx
// ✅
<AppHeading>Home</AppHeading>
aria-label="Main menu"

// ❌
<AppHeading>Головна</AppHeading>
aria-label="Головне меню"
```

## Keep it simple

- **Do not over-engineer** — pick the simplest solution that works for the current scope.
- **No speculative code** — no providers, listeners, abstractions, or desktop-only UX until they are actually needed.
- **Mobile-first** — skip click-outside, Escape handlers, hover-only flows, etc. unless explicitly requested.
- **Minimal diff** — do not add unrelated code when fixing or extending something.

## File granularity and placement

- **No micro-files** — do not add a new file for one small helper with a **single** call site. Put it in an existing `*Service.ts`, `config/*.ts`, file-local helpers at the bottom of the consumer, or merge related helpers into one domain service (e.g. `transactionCategoryService.ts` instead of two five-line files).
- **No one-off `features/<domain>/utils/`** — do not create a `utils/` folder under a feature for a lone function. Colocate with `config/`, `services/`, or the component that owns the behavior. Reserve `shared/utils/` for helpers reused across domains.
- **Config modules own their helpers** — constants and the pure functions that only serve them (palettes, stable color from id, label maps) live in the same `config/` file when small; do not split into a separate util file.

## Shared API list order

When a spec or API contract defines sort order (e.g. categories A→Z, system rows last):

- **Filter only** on the client — `filter` by kind/type; **preserve** the array order from `GET`.
- **Do not re-sort** on the client to “match” the server unless the product explicitly requires client-side ordering.
- After **POST/PATCH**, **invalidate/refetch** the list query; do not maintain a parallel sort algorithm.

## Cross-feature boundaries

- **Glue stays in the consumer feature** — mapping between two domains (e.g. `TransactionType` → `CategoryKind`, picker rules for transactions) lives in the feature that owns the screen/flow (`features/transactions/`), not in the shared domain module (`features/categories/`).
- **`features/<a>/` must not import `features/<b>/` types or UI** when `<b>` is the wrong direction (e.g. `categories` must not import `transactions`). The dependent feature imports the shared one.
- **Shared domain UI takes minimal props** — e.g. `CategoryIcon` accepts `iconKey` (+ `size`), not a full category row or transaction snapshot. If call sites want ergonomics (`category={…}`), add a **thin wrapper in the owning feature**, not a wider API on the shared component.

## Feature `types/` layout

- **Split API vs view models** — keep backend-shaped types (`Transaction`, request bodies, embedded nested objects) in a core types file; keep list/UI projections (`*ListViewItem`, action targets, filters) in a sibling file when the shape differs.
- **Merge only the same layer** — e.g. nested API object types belong with API types; swipe/edit targets can live with list view types. Do **not** dump view models, filters, and API DTOs into one mega file.
- **Names match the API/product** — use the name the API uses when unambiguous (e.g. `TransactionCategory` on a transaction payload), not `*Snapshot` / `*Embed` unless a second type with the same name already exists.
- **Type comments** — one short `//` line in plain English: what the type represents in the product/API. Avoid jargon (“embedded snapshot”, “camelCase from server”) when a plain sentence works.

```ts
// ✅
// Category id, name, icon, and kind as included on each transaction from the API.
export type TransactionCategory = { … };

// ❌
// Embedded category snapshot DTO (camelCase).
export type TransactionCategorySnapshot = { … };
```

## Imports and structure

- **No barrel `index.ts`** — import files directly: `@/pages/entry/EntryPage`, `@/shared/utils/twx`, `@/shared/services/storage/storageService`.
- Alias: `@/` → `frontend/src/`.
- **`app/`** — shell, routing, layout, navigation, global styles (not routable screens):
  - `App.tsx` — router root
  - `routing/` — route guards (`ProtectedAppRoute`); auth check + render layout or redirect
  - `layout/` — logged-in app chrome (`AppShell`: `<Outlet />`, tab bar, safe area); no own URL
  - `navigation/` — `routes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `useRouteNavigation`
  - `styles/` — `global.css`, `tokens.css`
- Pages: `pages/<name>/<Page>.tsx`, page-local pieces in subfolders as needed:
  - `components/` — page UI (forms, panels, tabs); default flat files (`LoginForm.tsx`). When the folder grows or has clear UI blocks, group by domain in subfolders (`amount/`, `details/`, `icons/`) — see `.cursor/rules/page-components-folders.mdc`. Never `LoginForm/LoginForm.tsx` mirror folders.
  - `hooks/` — page and form hooks
  - `api/` — page-scoped HTTP calls (e.g. `pages/auth/api/authApi.ts`)
  - `services/` — mappers, messages, page-scoped helpers
  - `types/` — form shapes, error codes, screen ids (`const` + derived `type`, e.g. `authScreen.ts`, `authErrorCodes.ts`)
  - `validation/` — client-side validators
  - `config/` — UI behavior constants only (motion variants, a11y ids) — not `const`+`type` enums; those go in `types/`
- **`features/`** — optional; extract domain here only when reused on **2+ screens**. Until then, keep logic in `pages/<name>/`.
- **Layer boundaries** — `pages/<a>/` must not import from `pages/<b>/` (another screen). Shared screen logic or UI used on 2+ routes → `features/<domain>/` (e.g. wallet list and bootstrap states → `features/wallets/`). Cross-tab month header chrome (`label` + month `title`) → `shared/ui/AppMonthPageHeader/`; page-specific accessories (e.g. Home wallet switcher) stay on that page. `features/*` must not import from `pages/*`. `app/navigation` must not import pages.
- **`shared/ui/`** — **PascalCase** folder = component name, same for the file inside: `AppButton/AppButton.tsx`, `EntryLayout/EntryLayout.tsx`. Import: `@/shared/ui/AppButton/AppButton`.
- **`App` prefix** — shared design-system components: `AppButton`, `AppField`, `AppHeading`… Exception: `Entry*` (entry funnel shell) — no `App`.
- **Larger `shared/ui` pieces** — same split as pages, but scoped to the component folder:
  - `ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx` — shell only: layout, wiring, composition; not every sub-piece inline
  - `components/` — subcomponents used only inside this UI piece; flat files (`TabLink.tsx`), group related sets in a subfolder (`components/icons/HomeTabIcon.tsx`)
  - `config/` — labels, maps, motion ids, other UI constants (`.ts` when possible; pass component refs, not inline JSX)
  - colocated helpers — `appTabBarMotion.ts`, small non-React utils next to the component when they belong to it only
- **Do not grow one file** — if a component file picks up distinct UI blocks (icons, buttons, config maps, helpers), extract them instead of stacking at the bottom of the main file. Split when pieces are separable, not only when the file is huge.

## Reusing `shared`

Before writing new UI or a utility in `pages/`, check whether something suitable already exists in `shared/`.

- **UI** — `shared/ui/` (`AppButton`, `AppField`, `AppHeading`, `AppTextButton`, `AppIcon`, `EntryLayout`…). If you need the same styles, markup, or behavior — import the existing piece; do not copy classes or markup into the page.
- **Bottom sheets / popups** — any mobile drawer overlay (slide-up panel, modal sheet, “popup” over the app) must use `AppPopup` from `@/shared/ui/AppPopup/AppPopup`. Do not import `vaul` / `Drawer` directly in pages or features; do not build custom `fixed inset-0` + `motion` sheet shells. Wrap flow-specific UI in a thin component (e.g. `HomeTransactionsPopup`, `AddTransactionPopup`) that composes `AppPopup` with `open` + `onOpenChange`. Use `AppPopupClose` / `AppPopupTitle` inside custom `header`; use `size`, `showHandle`, and `header` props before forking styles. Extend `AppPopup` when a new sheet variant is needed for multiple call sites — not one-off duplicates. **Exception:** anchored menus / dropdowns (e.g. wallet switcher) are not sheets — no `AppPopup`.
- **Utilities** — `shared/utils/` (`twx`, `timeUtils`…). Pure helpers without side effects. Do not duplicate locally in `pages/`.
- **Hooks** — `shared/hooks/` (`useScrollLock`, `useScreenTransition`…). Shared React hooks reused on 2+ screens or in app shell.
- **Browser** — `shared/browser/` (`isMobileBrowser`, `isPwaStandalone`…). UA / display-mode reads; call as plain functions, not hooks.
- **Services** — `shared/services/` (`storageService`, `appStorage`…). `storageService` — low-level `localStorage` access; `appStorage` — named getters/setters (`getWebsiteTesting`…).
- **New shared component** — when the same UI exists (or will exist) on **2+** screens, or it is a design-system primitive (button, field, heading). One-off UI unique to a single page — keep it in `pages/<name>/`.
- **Extend instead of copy** — if a shared component is close enough, add a prop (`size`, `className`) in `shared/ui` instead of forking a copy in the page.
- **Do not extract to shared for its own sake** — do not move a one-off decorative block or logic tied to a single flow into `shared/`.

```tsx
// ✅ app layer — guards and layout stay in app/, not pages/
import {ProtectedAppRoute} from "@/app/routing/ProtectedAppRoute";
import {AppShell} from "@/app/layout/AppShell";
import {HomePage} from "@/pages/home/HomePage";

// ❌ pages/app-shell/, pages/*Route*, layout shells mixed with screen pages
import {AppShell} from "@/pages/app-shell/AppShell";
```

```tsx
// ✅
import {AppButton} from "@/shared/ui/AppButton/AppButton";
import {AppField} from "@/shared/ui/AppField/AppField";

// ❌ custom button with the same classes in LoginForm
const LoginButton = () => (
  <button className="rounded-14 bg-e-btn-bg …">…</button>
);
```

```tsx
// ✅ sheet popup — AppPopup + controlled state in the parent that opens it
import {AppPopup} from "@/shared/ui/AppPopup/AppPopup";

export const ExamplePopup = ({open, onOpenChange}: Props) => (
  <AppPopup open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange} title="Recent">
    {children}
  </AppPopup>
);

// ❌ raw vaul or custom overlay sheet in a page
import {Drawer} from "vaul";
```

## Styles (Tailwind)

- Classes in JSX; **tokens from `app/styles/tokens.css`** (`text-15`, `size-38`, `rounded-11`) — avoid `text-[0.9375rem]` unless necessary.
- Conditional classes: `twx` from `@/shared/utils/twx`.
- Minimize arbitrary `[]` — rare selectors (`[&_strong]:…`). Safe-area padding/margin: use inset tokens from `tokens.css` (`pt-inset-top-page`, `pb-inset-bottom-tab`, …), not `max(..., env(safe-area-inset-*))` in JSX.
- Formatter: Biome, `bracketSpacing: false` → `{EntryPage}`, not `{ EntryPage }`.

## React

- Static values from device detection — plain constants, not `useState`, if they do not update:
  `const isIos = isIosBrowser();` instead of `useState(isIosBrowser)`.
- `useEffect(..., [])` — only for subscriptions/side effects, not for one-time UA reads.
- **No state updates during render** — render must be pure. Never call `setState`, `setTransition`, `dispatch`, etc. in the component/hook body. Update state in event handlers or effects instead. Mutating refs during render is fine.
- **React to prop/context changes** (pathname, outlet, flags) with `useLayoutEffect` when the UI must update before paint (animations), otherwise `useEffect`. Keep previous values in refs inside the effect.

```tsx
// ❌ setState while rendering
export const usePageSlideTransition = () => {
  const location = useLocation();
  const [transition, setTransition] = useState(null);
  const previousRef = useRef({pathname: location.pathname});

  if (location.pathname !== previousRef.current.pathname) {
    setTransition({from: previousRef.current.pathname, to: location.pathname});
    previousRef.current.pathname = location.pathname;
  }
};

// ✅ refs during render; setState in useLayoutEffect
export const usePageSlideTransition = () => {
  const location = useLocation();
  const outlet = useOutlet();
  const [transition, setTransition] = useState(null);
  const previousRef = useRef({pathname: location.pathname, outlet: null});

  if (outlet && location.pathname === previousRef.current.pathname) {
    previousRef.current.outlet = outlet;
  }

  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    if (location.pathname === previousRef.current.pathname) return;
    const from = previousRef.current;
    previousRef.current = {pathname: location.pathname, outlet};
    setTransition({from: from.pathname, to: location.pathname});
  }, [location.pathname, outlet]);
};
```

## Import example

```ts
import {AppShell} from "@/app/layout/AppShell";
import {EntryPage} from "@/pages/entry/EntryPage";
import {getWebsiteTesting} from "@/shared/services/storage/appStorage";
import {twx} from "@/shared/utils/twx";
import {isMobileBrowser} from "@/shared/browser/isMobileBrowser";
import {storageService} from "@/shared/services/storage/storageService";
```
